{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Gatherer of all the camps.</b> Since the tribe of Dan was numerous in population, it would travel last, and anyone who had lost something — it would restore it to him. This follows the one who says they journeyed in a written formation (כתיבה היו מהלכין). That is, it traveled on the north side, which was fixed for it, and since it was numerous in population, the people were spread out even across the entire west side, and because of this it would gather. And if you ask: is the banner of the camp of Judah not more numerous than its banner? One may answer that it was more numerous in population than the one that traveled last." "<b>Gatherer of all the camps.</b> Any person, even from the other banners, when he could not travel with his own banner, would gather with the banner of the camp of Dan, which was last. But no further could he remain, lest he be left alone. And therefore it calls it 'gatherer' — in the sense of ״and none gathers him homeward״ (ואין מאסף אותו הביתה)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:17.771140481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}